{"seconds": 60.3, "exit": 0, "final": "Good, so the bishop is defended by the queen. So Qc6+ moves the queen away from defending the bishop, but it also creates immediate tactical problems for White. This confirms the move is strong.\n\nLet me finalize my analysis:\n\n**Best Move: Qc6+** \n\nThis move forces the White king to move (or White must give up material). \n- If Kf1, Black plays Rxd1+ winning the bishop\n- If Kh3, Black has a strong attack\n- If Qe4, Qxe4+ wins the queen\n- If Bf3, Qxf3+ wins the bishop\n\nThe key pattern is using a forcing check to expose the king and win material or create a mating attack.\n\n**Coaching note (under 80 words):**\n\n\"Look for forcing checks that do double duty. Here, Qc6+ checks the king while attacking or threatening to capture undefended pieces. White's replies all lose material: if Kf1, your rook recapture Rxd1+ wins the bishop; if Qe4 blocks, Qxe4+ takes the queen; if Bf3, Qxf3+ wins the bishop. Always ask: after my forcing move, what's undefended?\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qc6+\", \"line\": [\"Qc6+\", \"Kf1\", \"Rxd1+\", \"Ke2\", \"Qc2+\", \"Kf3\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Q3KP/3B4 b - - 1 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Q3KP/3B4 b - - 1 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Q3KP/3B4 b - - 1 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Q3KP/3B4 b - - 1 43", "move": "Rd2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/6k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Qr2KP/3B4 w - - 2 44", "move": "Qxd2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/P1Q3KP/3B4 b - - 1 43", "move": "Qd4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/3r2k1/6pp/2q2p2/2P5/1R2b1P1/